# The second of rust's two aliased externals. `raw_string_literal_content`
# is emitted under the name `string_content`, so the external's own name
# cannot appear in any tree either.
#
# The claim is that a raw string keeps its backslashes: `r"a\b"` holds three
# content bytes, not two, and the `r` and both quotes stay outside them.
roots 1
mends 0
holds raw_string_literal
spans raw_string_literal 17 23
spans string_content 19 22
